Description: Add the missing 0.1.0a4 to 0.1.0a5 metadata transition
 Upstream 0.1.0a5 only changes version metadata. Its 0.1.0a4 and 0.1.0a5
 base SQL files are identical, so an empty transition safely lets existing
 installations advance their catalog version.
Author: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Forwarded: not-yet

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 HEADERS = src/spat.h
 
 DATA = sql/spat--0.1.0a5.sql
+DATA += sql/spat--0.1.0a4--0.1.0a5.sql
 
 PG_CPPFLAGS =
 
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sql/spat--0.1.0a4--0.1.0a5.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+-- spat 0.1.0a5 is a metadata-only release.
+-- The 0.1.0a4 and 0.1.0a5 base SQL files define identical objects, so no
+-- catalog changes are required for this transition.
